WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.960 --> 00:00:07.380
As AI and high performance computing workloads continue to scale,

2
00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:12.200
the power and cooling demands of modern data centers are

3
00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:17.800
reaching unprecedented levels. The Open Compute Project's High Power

4
00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:23.520
Rack, or HPR, addresses this challenge by extending the

5
00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:28.520
ORv3 standard to meet next -generation power requirements, without

6
00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:33.260
disrupting the foundational modularity that makes ORv3 so scalable.

7
00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:37.280
The motivation behind HPR is clear.

8
00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:42.820
Standard ORv3 racks typically support up to 18 to 36

9
00:00:42.820 --> 00:00:47.640
kilowatts per rack. But with dense GPU and AI -accelerated

10
00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:52.600
deployments, operators are now pushing toward 100 kilowatts and beyond,

11
00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:54.980
towards the 1 megawatt rack.

12
00:00:56.120 --> 00:00:59.720
This doubling of power density demands more than just bigger

13
00:00:59.720 --> 00:01:03.980
power supplies. It requires a rack ecosystem rethink.

14
00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:08.000
That's where HPR comes in.

15
00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:13.000
It retains the same physical envelope and mechanical alignment as

16
00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:17.220
the base ORv3 standard, meaning you don't have to redesign

17
00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:18.500
your data center layout.

18
00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:25.700
Instead, HPR introduces enhanced features inside the rack to safely

19
00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:29.480
deliver higher power and manage thermal output more efficiently.

20
00:01:30.760 --> 00:01:34.920
The cornerstone of the ORv3 that continues with the HPR

21
00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:39.360
design is its adoption of 48V direct power distribution.

22
00:01:40.180 --> 00:01:44.160
Carried through a higher current, deeper designed busbar systems supported

23
00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:46.780
by a new extension to the back of the frame.

24
00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:51.840
This approach not only supports more powerful IT gear, but

25
00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:55.620
also improves energy efficiency by reducing conversion losses.

26
00:01:56.700 --> 00:02:01.000
New busbar extensions and grounding enhancements ensure safety and

27
00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:04.600
compatibility with OCP's evolving electrical architecture.

28
00:02:05.420 --> 00:02:08.220
But delivering more power is only half the story.

29
00:02:08.860 --> 00:02:14.060
The HPR solution also addresses the thermal challenge by integrating

30
00:02:14.060 --> 00:02:16.140
blindmate liquid cooling manifolds.

31
00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:21.720
These front -accessible modular cooling interfaces support cold plate

32
00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:25.820
loops directly within the rack, making it easier to manage

33
00:02:25.820 --> 00:02:28.040
heat generated by high wattage components.

34
00:02:28.700 --> 00:02:33.300
The design reduces reliance on traditional air cooling, helping facilities

35
00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:37.220
scale without exceeding environmental or HVAC limits.

36
00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:42.820
Importantly, HPR achieves all of this while remaining part of

37
00:02:42.820 --> 00:02:44.560
the broader ORv3 family.

38
00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:47.080
It's not a standalone solution.

39
00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:51.520
It's a high -power extension of a standard already in

40
00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:57.020
global deployment. That means facilities can gradually adopt HPR

41
00:02:57.020 --> 00:03:01.420
elements as their workload demands increase, without replacing their

42
00:03:01.420 --> 00:03:07.140
entire infrastructure. HPR was well -introduced at the OCP Global

43
00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:11.640
Summit in 2024, to support 92 kW or more.

44
00:03:12.500 --> 00:03:16.040
But since then, it's quickly evolving within the rack and

45
00:03:16.040 --> 00:03:20.900
power OCP projects community, through multiple iterations, with plans

46
00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:23.900
to now go to 1600 roofline rack power.

47
00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:28.680
In short, the high -power rack represents OCP's vision of

48
00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:32.640
an AI -ready, thermally resilient, and energy -optimized future.

49
00:03:33.800 --> 00:03:38.040
It allows data centers to meet rising demands without sacrificing

50
00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:42.620
the open, interoperable principles that ORv3 is built on.

